/T (In other sub-regional contexts, this initial wave of regionalism also gave rise to the establishment of the Common Market of the Central America \(MCCA\) \(1960\), the Andean Pact \(1969\), the Caribbean Community \(1973\), and the Organization of the East Caribbean States \(1981\). These economic integration processes had different initial objectives: creating a free trade zone, a customs union or a common market. This was at the time seen as a gradual and linear movement, following the European Community developments. )
/E (In other sub-regional contexts, this initial wave of regionalism also gave rise to the establishment of the Common Market of the Central America \(MCCA\) \(1960\), the Andean Pact \(1969\), the Caribbean Community \(1973\), and the Organization of the East Caribbean States \(1981\). These economic integration processes had different initial objectives: creating a free trade zone, a customs union or a common market. This was at the time seen as a gradual and linear movement, following the European Community developments. )
