/S /H2
/P 215 0 R
/T (The EU's influence on continental and sub-regional integration remains substantial yet ambiguous. Currently, trade relations with the EU are partially governed by Economic Partnership Agreements \(EPAs\), which have been negotiated at the sub-regional rather than the continental level. Five EPAs, covering 14 AU member states, are in operation. However, this fragmented tariff and regulatory framework complicates the implementation of the AfCFTA. Additionally, approximately 30 African countries, categorized as Least Developed Countries \(LDCs\), benefit from tariff-free access to the EU market. )
/E (The EU's influence on continental and sub-regional integration remains substantial yet ambiguous. Currently, trade relations with the EU are partially governed by Economic Partnership Agreements \(EPAs\), which have been negotiated at the sub-regional rather than the continental level. Five EPAs, covering 14 AU member states, are in operation. However, this fragmented tariff and regulatory framework complicates the implementation of the AfCFTA. Additionally, approximately 30 African countries, categorized as Least Developed Countries \(LDCs\), benefit from tariff-free access to the EU market. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
