638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 229 0 R
/T (An important issue in this peace and security partnership has been the dependence of the RECs and, to a lesser extent, the AU on EU funding for the deployment of PSOs and other security programmes \(Engel, 2020\). In the case of the RECs it generally accounts for more than 60% of their operational funding \(Mattheis et al., 2023\). This dependence fuels the structural asymmetry of the relationship which might be further reinforced by the creation of the EPF and the NDICI, as well as the growing prominence of trust funds such as the EUTFA, none of which rely on join governance and decision-making, thus implying less African participation \(ONGD, 2021\). Interestingly, while this asymmetry in the peace and security partnership has led to complaints from African actors that the EU is forcing their hands and seeking to shape the African security agenda, there has been a perception in EU circles that the EU has little influence relative to their status as the largest funder \(Staeger, 2023\). )
/E (An important issue in this peace and security partnership has been the dependence of the RECs and, to a lesser extent, the AU on EU funding for the deployment of PSOs and other security programmes \(Engel, 2020\). In the case of the RECs it generally accounts for more than 60% of their operational funding \(Mattheis et al., 2023\). This dependence fuels the structural asymmetry of the relationship which might be further reinforced by the creation of the EPF and the NDICI, as well as the growing prominence of trust funds such as the EUTFA, none of which rely on join governance and decision-making, thus implying less African participation \(ONGD, 2021\). Interestingly, while this asymmetry in the peace and security partnership has led to complaints from African actors that the EU is forcing their hands and seeking to shape the African security agenda, there has been a perception in EU circles that the EU has little influence relative to their status as the largest funder \(Staeger, 2023\). )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
