/T ([6] It is important to note that the WVS did not conduct the survey inall waves in every country or ask all questions consistently. This limits our ability to draw definitive comparisons between countries. However, the data remains systematic, providing valuable insights, making it possible to identify trends, regional patterns and, at some point, shifts in public opinion and trust over time.)
/E ([6] It is important to note that the WVS did not conduct the survey inall waves in every country or ask all questions consistently. This limits our ability to draw definitive comparisons between countries. However, the data remains systematic, providing valuable insights, making it possible to identify trends, regional patterns and, at some point, shifts in public opinion and trust over time.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [7]
>>
